+// by position (the bottom one, Switch B, is south: GameCube A), ZR the right
+// shoulder (GameCube Z), L or ZL the left trigger and R the right trigger
+// (GameCube L and R). A single Joy-Con is held sideways: its stick turns with
+// it, its face buttons keep their positions in the hand, SL and SR are the
+// triggers. A GameCube controller (the USB adapter) keeps its own labels,
+// with Z (reported as R) and its analog triggers.
 
